3.2.b
Demolition Notes
As stated in the SA, the structural framing along the two-story west wall of the Carey Building appears to
frame into and bear on the adjacent building along a majority of the west wall. The joists appear to be
pocketed into the wall, no physical attachment of the joist to the wall was observed. Therefore, it appears
that the Carey Building can be demolished without compromising the structural integrity of the adjacent
building.
Selective demolition should still be performed in the area to confirm there is no physical
attachment prior to full demolition.
It is important to note that if the new building on this Site does not extend to the same height as the existing
structure proposed to be demolished, there may be some repair façade work needed to the building
adjacent to the west. This has been accounted for in the Project Cost Model.
