04
2018 PHASE
I ESA REVIEW
This section will provide a brief overview the 2018 Trihydro Phase
ESA (Appendix A) and the suggested
solution to remedy the environmental conditions of concern.
The cover letter for this report from Trihydro, provides an overall summary of the report findings:
Bused upon the findings in the Phase 1 ESA, Trihydro does nat believe that a Phase II ESA is
warranted at this time.
The RECs, HRECs, and CRECs that were identified at off-site
properties do not appear to pose a subsurface concern to the Site.
As noted, the most
significant business environmental risk at this time is the confirmed presence of asbestos
containing materials.
The Phase I ESA was intended to reduce, but not eliminate, uncertainty regarding the potential for
environmental concerns for this Site. Due to a Phase II ESA not being recommended, the findings
in Phase
I
will be reviewed and assessed accordingly; solutions to remedy the known
