Due to the age of the 2006 Terracon ACM Survey, NGA contacted Linda Dewitt, Asbestos Program
Coordinator, Wyoming Department of Environmental Quality, to confirm that the ACM Survey could be
considered valid and received the following information:
An inspection is valid as long as it covers the building materials that are still
present in the building
Often, asbestos inspections are performed to
determine if current bui(ding finishes at the time contain asbestos and then
renovation is performed to change or remove those finishes. Ifyou can prove
(by photos or written statement from the original inspector) that the
materials present are the same materials that the original inspector
examined, then that inspection can be used.
if new or replacement materials were installed after the previous inspection,
then only those new/replacement materials would have to be inspected to
determine if they are suspect and potentially sampied.
The City hired Terracon to update and complete the 2006 Terracon ACM Survey to meet the WDEQ
requirement. The findings of Terracon’s updated ACM Survey are included in Appendix B and discussed in
section 4.2.d Asbestos Containing Materials - BER.
