2OlSAyres Associates Phase 1 ESA: Cheyenne PCE Plume CERCLIS site, located near West 26th Street
and Pioneer Avenue. This plume is mapped approximately 038 miles north of the subject property
and extends at least as far south as West 22 Street, which is 0.3 miles northeast of the subject
property. According to WDEQ staff, there is a second orphan site plume located to the northwest
that is not listed on regulatory databa5e at this time.
•
2016 Ayres Associates Phase I ESA: The subject property’s down-gradient location in proximity to
the Cheyenne PCE Plume CERCLIS site is considered to be a REC. The extent of groundwater and
vapor impacts is currently unknown but reach at least as far south as West 22 Street, 0.3 miles
northeast of the subject property. Additionally, an interview with WDEQ staff indicates a second
smaller orphan plume several blocks northwest of the subject property, but the extent of impacts
has not yet been documented. These factors suggest the likely presence of groundwater and soil
vapor contaminated with chlorinated solvents at the subject property.
To address the issue of the potential impacts of the Cheyenne PCE Plume on this Site, a Vapor Intrusion
Barrier and Ventilation System will be incorporated into the design and construction of this project.
4.2.b
Regulatory Agency Review— RECs and ARECs
Numerous surrounding properties were identified within regulatory databases with open or unresolved
environmental issues that are identified as REC5 and HRECs with respect to the site. Trihydro stated that it
appears that this Site has numerous potential for impacts to indoor air quality and a vapor encroachment
concerns (VEC), however indoor air quality and vapor screening were not performed.
To address the issue of the potential impacts of the surrounding properties on this Site, a Vapor Intrusion
Barrier and Ventilation System will be incorporated into the design and construction of this project.
4.2.c
Vapor Intrusion Exposures - REC
Numerous surrounding properties have been identified with open unresolved petroleum hydrocarbon and
chemicals of concern impacts that pose a REC to the Site regarding indoor air quality. It is important to note
that indoor air quality and vapor screening were not performed in the 2018 Trihydro Phase I ESA.
