summary of the 2018 Terracon ACM Survey:
‘
The materials that were identified to be Category I non-friable ACM and may remain in the building
during demolition provided the materials remain non-friable during demolition are: Gray Roof Tar
(Ri and R2), Flashing (Ri), and Black Tar, Felt and Yellow Insulation (Ri alcove). If these materials
are likely to become friable during demolition, they must be abated prior to demolition activities.
•
The materials that were identified to be Category II non-friable ACM are: Gray Caulk on Metal
Flashing (Ri), White Window Caulk on Ground Level Windows, Marble Façade Grout on Exterior
Façade, Exterior Stucco Soffit on Ground Level Entrances, Door Window Glazing on Exterior Alley
Doors, R2 Door, and R3 Door, and Basement Door Room 25. These materials are likely to become
friable due to demolition activities and should therefore be considered regulated ACM and be
abated prior to demolition.
