6.3
DEMOLITION & ABATEMENT
The goal of the demolition portion of this Project is to remove the existing structure on this Site, including
abatement of ACM materials as required, and to prepare a clean, level site suitable for new construction.
6.3.a
Demolition Cost Estimates
What should be included in the basic demolition cost estimate: full building demolition and removal of all
debris, saw-cutting as required, import clean Istructural fill material for backfill, compaction and compaction
testing, water truck for dust control, erosion control, weather protection, water and sewer disconnects at
property line, permitting, traffic control, and basic bond and insurance requirements.
The following items are assumed to not be included in the estimates below: Asbestos, Freon, and other
hazardous material removal, Structural Shoring, daily air sampling, Site Surveying, and repair work on the
adjacent building.
Asbestos Abatement is a separate budget line item that will include Structural Shoring. Site Surveying and
Soils Testing is typically provided by the Owner and is included in Soft Costs. There is freon in some of the
mechanical equipment on this Site, $4,000 will be used as a budgetary value for removal of this item. A
budgetary value of $15,000 will be used for the repair work on the adjacent building. For the daily air
sampling throughout the full building demo, a budgetary value of $25,000 will be used.
Redco Construction:
Included in Weaver and Affinity Site Proposal (Appendix A). The cost estimate looks
to be inclusive of the major elements of this portion of the Project. The Asbestos
Abatement estimate will not be included in the demolition cost estimate for
comparison value. Deducting the abatement portion from the bid, and adding the
freon, repair to adjacent building, and daily air sampling allowances brings the
adjusted demolition cost estimate to: $1,191,566.38
Rocky Mtn Demolition: Provided by the City (Appendix F). Exclusions to this bid include: traffic control, all
site facilities, shoring, sitework, temporary utilities, saw-toothing, and weather
protection, among others.
It does specifically include demolition and removal of
